in the description.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.240
As if it wasn't bad enough already that

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.420
people have fallen ill
from the coronavirus,

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.610
businesses are closing, quarantines,

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.080
and some states are on complete lockdown,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.660
now we have senators
allegedly profiteering

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.720
off of this worldwide pandemic.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.450
Four senators have now been
alleged to have engaged

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.870
in insider trading by
liquidating or trading stocks

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.760
just weeks before a massive
sell-off in the market

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.120
due to coronavirus panic.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.330
Senators Richard Burr, Kelly
Loeffler, Dianne Feinstein,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.870
and Jim Inhofe have all been
accused of selling stocks

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.860
after getting inside information.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.760
Two of the four, Burr and Loeffler,

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.730
took part in a classified
and non-public hearing

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.650
regarding the coronavirus
and its looming impact.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.880
Those two senators, Richard Burr,

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.030
a senator from North Carolina and chairman

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.680
of the Senate Intelligence Committee,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.930
and Kelly Loeffler, a newly
appointed senator from Georgia,

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:01.060
sold significant amounts
of stock at the same time

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.010
they were receiving non-public
classified information

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.100
about the severity of the coronavirus

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.670
and its potential
devastating impact worldwide,

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.280
at the same time that they
may have been downplaying

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.000
the effects of the
coronavirus to the public.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.600
If these allegations are
true, is this a crime?

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.162
Well, we're about to find out.

00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:21.995
(dramatic music)

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.630
Hey legal eagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer,

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.050
and maybe get out the
pitchforks and guillotines,

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:31.070
because it might be time for
some senatorial heads to roll.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.680
Today, we're going to discuss what happens

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.330
when senators abuse their position

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.280
and profit off of a massive tragedy,

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.100
or is this all just a
big misunderstanding?

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.660
Now, to better understand what
Senators Burr and Loeffler

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.310
are being accused of,
it'll be helpful to have

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.760
a little background as to
what insider trading is,

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.020
and how it developed
into its current form.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.820
The Securities and Exchange
Act of 1934 was enacted

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.580
with a desire to promote fairness

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.270
and clarity in the federal securities laws

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.390
for all participants in
the financial market.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.030
Section 10b of the Exchange
Act was intended to be

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.250
the Exchange Act's broad
anti-fraud provision

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.220
designed to cover the full range
of fraudulent conduct that,

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.630
quote, "human ingenuity can devise."

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.560
Of course, humans are very ingenuitive

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.680
when it comes to defrauding other people.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.590
The Supreme Court has
recognized that 10b was designed

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.520
as a catch-all clause to
prevent fraudulent practices.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.600
Now, it's from this
statute that the concept

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.140
of insider trading was born.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.580
Although the concept of insider
trading emerged in the '60s,

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.360
it really wasn't until the 1980s
that the U.S. Supreme Court

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.500
affirmed that insider trading was in fact

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.870
a violation of section 10b.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.830
After insider trading was deemed legal,

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.070
what developed were sort
of two types and reasons

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.370
for insider trading, the classical theory,

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.990
and the more expansive
misappropriation theory.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.820
Now, the classical
theory of insider trading

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.440
specifically holds that
corporate insiders are liable

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.970
when they use material
non-public information

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.850
obtained from their unique
position within a corporation

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.710
for their own personal advantage
in the securities market.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.670
As the SEC has noted there
is an inherent unfairness

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:57.260
in allowing a corporate insider to use

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.410
non-public information to the detriment

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:01.840
of other innocent investors
in securities markets.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.130
The Supreme Court has
reasoned that an individual

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.630
must refrain from trading securities

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.630
on the basis of non-public information

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.740
because of their fiduciary relationship

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.010
with shareholders as a corporate insider.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:15.190
Now, that really only applies
to corporate insiders,

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.640
and you can imagine that there's all kinds

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.690
of insider trading that
doesn't actually involve

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.960
someone inside the company itself,

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.870
which is why the Supreme
Court later adopted

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.700
what's now known as the
misappropriation theory

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.840
of insider trading,
which extended liability

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.060
to certain corporate outsiders that traded

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.610
on confidential information
in breach of some duty

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:33.990
owed to the source of information,

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:36.480
not necessarily the
shareholders themselves.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.560
The Supreme Court has held that

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.080
under a misappropriation
theory an individual breaches

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.100
a duty to the owner of
confidential information

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.790
by using that information
to his or her advantage

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.000
in the stock market.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.270
It's called misappropriation theory

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.690
because it's kind of like stealing.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.290
You are taking information
that doesn't belong to you

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.980
and using it for your own advantage.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.670
This often comes up in what are called

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.650
tipper or tippee cases,
essentially one who receives

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:02.460
an inside tip and trades
that non-public information

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.510
received from a tipper, they're
liable under Section 10b

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.510
of the Exchange Act,
regardless of whether or not

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.920
there was any benefit to the person

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.070
that provided the tip itself.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:12.810
Now, that's all in the corporate context,

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.780
but what about members of Congress?

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:16.890
Congresspeople are privy to a whole host

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:19.050
of classified and non-public information

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.440
that most of us are completely unaware of.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.070
They're not corporate insiders
in the classical sense,

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.170
but they still have
information at their fingertips

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.910
that can easily be used for
their own personal gain.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.230
So what happens when
someone in Congress makes

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.170
an investment decision in the stock market

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:36.210
based on this potentially classified

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.760
or top secret information?

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.880
Would they be liable under
some form of insider trading?

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.730
Well, the answer for a long
time was effectively no.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:47.520
Congress basically had this
absurd loophole that made

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.500
insider trading legal and even above board

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.000
with congressional ethics rules.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.970
This is what happens when
the rule makers make rules

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:57.580
about themselves, and the statistics show

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.510
just how advantageous this was for them.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:02.410
While traders were beating
the market by approximately 5%

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.860
and hedge funds by seven to 8%,

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.080
in one study published by
the Journal of Financial

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.720
and Quantitative Analysis it
showed that congresspeople

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.210
were beating the market
by an astounding 12%,

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.770
and what's even more
astounding than their returns

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:19.550
is Congress' brazenness with
which they were cashing in.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.040
Former Senator John
Kerry is a prime example

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.840
of cashing in on non-public information.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.870
For instance, on May 15,
2007 the government ended

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.320
reimbursements of an obscure
anemia drug manufactured

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.810
by Amgen which caused the
company's stock to tank,

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.420
but you know who sold
all of their Amgen stock

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.330
just days before?

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:40.070
Yup, that's right, former
presidential candidate

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.240
Senator John Kerry.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.060
He avoided almost any loss by selling

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:45.840
all of his stock on May 4th and May 5th,

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.810
just days before the reimbursements ended.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:50.350
Impeccable timing, of course.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.640
Kerry had similar good fortune

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.720
when it came to the rollout of Obamacare.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.530
Kerry was a member of the
Senate Finance Committee

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.930
Subcommittee on Health and
played a key role in developing

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:01.400
President Obama's healthcare
reform legislation.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.190
- It isn't about eating broccoli, folks.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:06.730
- And just prior to the
enactment of the ACA

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:10.250
Kerry bought stock in big
time winners that resulted

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.340
from Obamacare, such as
pharmaceutical companies Teva

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:16.050
and ResMed, a medical device manufacturer,

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.300
and at the same time, Kerry dumped stock

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.800
in the health insurance
industry, which suffered greatly

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.050
as a result of the passage of Obamacare.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:25.900
However, no example is
worse or more appalling

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.520
than that a former
Representative Spencer Bachus.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.047
During the financial crisis of 2008,

00:06:30.047 --> 00:06:31.550
Bachus was a ranking member

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:33.280
on the Financial Services Committee,

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:36.840
and on September 18, 2008 Bachus
received a private briefing

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:39.020
on the collapsing economy
and financial system

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.470
from none other than the
chairman of the Federal Reserve

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:42.550
at the time Ben Bernanke,

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.700
and the Treasury Secretary Hank Paulson.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.950
Armed with information that
practically no one else

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:50.200
knew about, what else could
Bachus possibly do with it?

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:53.130
Well, he invested heavily
in the market failing.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:55.550
Bachus effectively shorted
the market by buying options

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.040
that would only rise if the market tanked,

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:01.460
and a few days later the market
went down as anticipated,

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:03.760
and Bachus nearly doubled his money.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.560
So in an attempt to clear
up Congress' responsibility

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.420
under the Exchange Act
and a natural extension

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:09.940
of the misappropriation theory,

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.480
Congress passed what is
known as the STOCK Act.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.780
The STOCK Act is short
for the Stop Trading

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.540
On Congressional Knowledge Act,

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.840
and was passed in April of 2012

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.400
during the presidency of Barack Obama,

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.730
and it made it illegal
for members of Congress

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.590
to make investment decisions
based on non-public information

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:28.400
they obtained in their
unique political positions.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.580
That is, you can't make
trades in the stock market

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:33.130
based on classified information
received in meetings

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.870
and briefings that were
meant to aid politicians

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.720
in making decisions for
the good of the public.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.510
Now, prior to this act the
SEC held that government

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:43.470
information had no connection
with insider trading.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.170
Of course you might say that as well

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:47.330
if the people using this
information were also

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.310
the same people that
controlled your funding,

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.780
but this hugely bipartisan
bill was supported

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.740
by a vote of 96 to three.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.040
Only three senators voted against this act

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.560
that would prohibit Congress
from financially benefiting

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.290
off of classified information.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:03.510
Of course, one of those
three senators, ironically,

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:06.800
was Senator Richard
Burr, who, as we noted,

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.730
is currently being accused
of insider trading himself.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.870
You really can't make this up.

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:14.540
So let's talk about
the illustrious senator

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.560
from the great state of North Carolina.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.910
Senator Richard Burr was recently privy

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.960
to classified information
about how potentially dangerous

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.330
and devastating the
coronavirus outbreak could be,

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:26.350
way before it was on
the radar of any of us

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:28.020
everyday folks in the United States.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.040
In addition to being a senator with access

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.680
to significant amount of
classified information

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:35.780
on the coronavirus, Burr himself
had a unique understanding

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.700
of what was going on because
of his role as the chairman

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.290
of the Senate Intelligence Committee

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.350
and the daily briefings on the
coronavirus that he received.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.860
In fact, Burr might be
considered something of an expert

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:47.990
in biohazard threats and
actually helped to write

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.900
the Pandemic and All-Hazards
Preparedness Act,

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.230
which forms the framework
for the federal response

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:55.640
to the very situation that
we're dealing with right now

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:57.000
in terms of the coronavirus.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.700
So what did Burr do with
this vital information,

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.210
and his unique expertise?

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.630
Did he warn the public
and ensure them that

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:05.990
despite the administration's
downplaying of the threat

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:08.580
that the American public was
aware of what was going on,

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.960
so that they could be
prepared as best as possible?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.730
No, it doesn't seem so.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.800
It seems that around
the time that Burr was

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.310
first made aware of this information

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:18.640
on potential future
impact of the coronavirus

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:22.740
he sold off nearly $1.6 million
of his stocks portfolio.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.380
In fact, on one day alone, February 13th,

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.567
Burr sold personal stocks
worth between 628,000

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:33.567
and $1.72 million in 33
separate transactions.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.810
To give you a frame of
reference, that is the most stock

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:38.800
he's sold in a single day in 14 months.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.450
His timing was of course impeccable,

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.610
as a week after Burr's sales

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.810
the stock market began a sharp decline

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:47.890
and has lost at least 30%
of its value ever since.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:50.200
And what makes this even more
interesting is that not only

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.500
did he sell a bunch of
personal stocks at this time,

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.890
large quantities of those
sales were in industries

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:57.550
that have been hit significantly
hard by the pandemic,

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:01.480
like $150,000 in the Wyndham
Hotel and Resorts stock,

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.730
which has lost nearly 2/3 of its value.

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:06.120
In fact, Burr shared some
of this inside information

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:09.180
of dire economic and societal
effects to only a select few

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.520
in late February, while
President Trump was

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.250
actively downplaying any
fears about COVID-19.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:17.120
- This is a list of the
different countries.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.950
The United States is rated
number one most prepared.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:23.300
- On February 27th, Burr addressed a group

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.810
at the Tar Heel Circle
about the potential impact

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:26.690
of the coronavirus.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:28.510
In addressing companies and organizations

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:31.280
from North Carolina that
donated more than $100,000

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.650
to his election campaign Burr said--

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:34.818
- [Richard] There's one
thing that I can tell you

00:10:34.818 --> 00:10:37.550
about this, it is much more
aggressive in its transmission

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:41.820
than anything that we have
seen in recent history.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:45.530
It's probably more akin
to the 1918 pandemic.

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:49.456
Every company should be
cognizant of the fact that

00:10:49.456 --> 00:10:51.820
you may have to alter your travel.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:53.400
You may have to look at your employees

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.490
and judge whether the trip
they're making to Europe

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.350
is essential, or whether it can
be done on video conference.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:00.550
Why risk it?

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.707
- Burr went on to say,
"there will be, I'm sure,

00:11:02.707 --> 00:11:05.707
"times that communities,
probably some in North Carolina,

00:11:05.707 --> 00:11:07.697
"have a transmission rate where they say

00:11:07.697 --> 00:11:09.447
"'let's close schools for two weeks,

00:11:09.447 --> 00:11:10.920
"'everybody stay home.'"

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.900
These statements were made 13 days

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.890
before the U.S. State
Department warned Americans

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:17.010
against international travel
and more than two weeks

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.960
before North Carolina
decided to close its schools.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.030
In an apparent attempt to
diffuse these allegations,

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:23.887
a spokesman for Senator Burr stated,

00:11:23.887 --> 00:11:26.147
"Senator Burr filed a
financial disclosure form

00:11:26.147 --> 00:11:28.087
"for personal transactions
made several weeks

00:11:28.087 --> 00:11:30.807
"before the U.S. and
financial markets showed signs

00:11:30.807 --> 00:11:33.900
"of volatility due to the
growing coronavirus outbreak."

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:36.770
The thing is that's sort of
what he's being accused of.

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:39.690
It looks like he knew
what was going to happen

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.120
before a lot of other people did,

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.700
and then sold off the stocks.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:46.370
Whether he disclosed the sale later on

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:48.660
isn't material to whether he traded

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.740
on inside congressional information.

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:52.590
By the way, I asked for recommendations

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:54.930
for targeted and effective
charities regarding

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:56.290
the coronavirus on Twitter,

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.690
and you legal eagles did not disappoint.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.350
I wanted to highlight one of them here,

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:03.130
the Gates Foundation COVID-19 Fund.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:06.200
They focus on vaccines,
diagnostics, and therapeutics,

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:09.240
which are going to be necessary
for ending this pandemic.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.140
In fact, there are
several funds that you can

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:13.250
choose from to get even more targeted,

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.050
and the Gates Foundation has
had a jump start on most of us

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:19.190
since they started focusing
on the coronavirus in January,

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:21.860
and they have general
expertise in global health

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:23.280
and biomedical research.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:24.720
I'll drop a link in the description.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:26.780
I just gave $500.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.330
If you're in a position to give,

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:30.520
I would really appreciate it if you could.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:33.710
But onto the next
criminal, I mean, senator.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.730
Now, Senator Burr wasn't the only one

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.970
potentially getting in on the action

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:39.760
of trading on inside information.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:40.920
Another interesting case is that

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:43.680
of newly appointed senator
Kelly Loeffler from Georgia,

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:47.090
who is potentially the richest
member in Congress right now.

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:49.640
Loeffler, whose husband, Jeffrey Sprecher,

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:52.900
is the chairman of the
New York Stock Exchange,

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:56.030
she began aggressively selling
equities on January 24th,

00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:58.450
the same day that she was present
for an all Senate briefing

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:00.540
conducted with the CDC director

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.750
and officials from the
National Institute of Allergy

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:04.100
and Infectious Diseases.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.910
Over the next few weeks, she and Sprecher

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:10.840
sold stock to the tune of
potentially $3,000,000,

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:13.250
and it's important to
note that from January 6th

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.890
when she was selected to take
the place of Senator Isakson

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.680
until the day of this coronavirus briefing

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:21.360
Loeffler had not made a
single stock transaction.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.760
From that day through the
middle of February, however,

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:26.490
her household dumped seven
figures worth of stocks

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.330
in almost 30 separate transactions.

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:30.620
Additional SEC filings
showed that Sprecher sold

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:33.230
an additional 3.5 million in
shares of his own company,

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:35.960
Intercontinental Exchange, on February 26,

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.300
which is also Loeffler's former employer.

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:40.400
The power couple then
went on to sell another

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.200
15.3 million shares in the
same company on March 11th,

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.770
and since the initial sale of their stock

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:49.470
in Intercontinental Exchange
the company's stock prices

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.720
almost dropped 25%.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.130
They then conveniently
bought shares in Citrix,

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:56.440
a company which makes
teleworking software.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:58.560
At the same time, there
have also been allegations

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.230
against Senator Feinstein and Inhofe

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.950
who have been accused of dubiously selling

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:04.390
large amounts of stocks in the weeks prior

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:06.830
to the markets reaction
to the coronavirus.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.500
Those Senators Feinstein and
Inhofe were not in attendance

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.710
of the all Senate briefing
on the coronavirus

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:14.280
that Loeffler and Burr were present for.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.080
In addition, Senator
Feinstein indicated that

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:18.280
her investments are actually
held in a blind trust

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:21.620
that she has no control
over or even any oversight.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.560
That being said, the
timing of these trades

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:26.350
still raises questions that
should probably be investigated.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:27.590
We lose sight of this sometimes,

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.440
but the mere appearance of impropriety

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.870
shakes people's faith in our institution.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.510
But those are the allegations
against the four senators,

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:37.460
though really we're only
hearing one side of this story,

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:40.530
sourced largely from a Daily
Beast article on this topic.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:43.140
But what are the potential
defenses that these senators

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:46.560
might have to raise against
allegations of insider trading?

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.640
Well, of course you have
the standard insider trading

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:51.040
defenses, such as the fact
that there was a disclosure

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:53.370
prior to the use of the
material information,

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.910
or a lack of knowledge that
the material information

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.650
was actually confidential.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:59.870
Other straightforward
defenses can be used as well,

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.730
like the argument that the
person never actually had

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:04.600
possession of material
non-public information,

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.600
or the classic my lawyer
said it was okay defense,

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:10.770
and courts have found
insider trading did not occur

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:12.730
when the transaction
was part of a scheduled

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:14.710
or predetermined trading plan,

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:17.020
and we don't necessarily know what

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:18.830
any of these particular senators had

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.250
in terms of financial planning.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:22.710
There's actually a constitutional
defense that may be made

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:24.590
by members of Congress
too under what's known

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.350
as the Speech and Debate Clause.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:27.817
The text in the Constitution says that

00:15:27.817 --> 00:15:30.190
"for any speech or debate in either House"

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:32.417
members of Congress
"shall not be questioned

00:15:32.417 --> 00:15:33.750
"in any other place."

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.880
That clause has been
interpreted to provide a certain

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.890
criminal and civil immunity for lawmakers

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:40.790
when they're engaging in
official legislative acts.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.550
That rule has been used
by members of Congress

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:44.140
to refuse to answer subpoenas,

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:46.500
and it would be pretty
likely that they would do so

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.380
if the SEC attempts to investigate
any of these allegations,

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.230
particularly if it has to
do with information that

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:54.190
they received in briefings
on the coronavirus.

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:56.810
Now, the factual defenses that
Burr and Loeffler have raised

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.620
come from a couple of different angles.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:00.490
Loeffler simply contends that she simply

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.370
didn't make the trades
and that they were done

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:04.630
by a third party financial advisor.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:07.887
Loeffler defended herself
on Twitter by saying,

00:16:07.887 --> 00:16:09.967
"this is a ridiculous and baseless attack.

00:16:09.967 --> 00:16:13.037
"I do not make investment
decisions for my portfolio.

00:16:13.037 --> 00:16:15.407
"Investment decisions are made by multiple

00:16:15.407 --> 00:16:17.047
"third party advisors without my,

00:16:17.047 --> 00:16:19.267
"or my husband's,
knowledge or involvement.

00:16:19.267 --> 00:16:22.177
"As confirmed in the
periodic transaction report

00:16:22.177 --> 00:16:25.477
"to Senate Ethics, I was
informed of these purchases

00:16:25.477 --> 00:16:27.907
"and sales on February 16, 2020,

00:16:27.907 --> 00:16:29.840
"three weeks after they were made."

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.440
- If you actually look at the
personal transaction reports

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.440
that were filed, it
notices at the bottom that

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:37.910
I'm only informed of my transactions

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:39.840
after they occur, several weeks.

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:41.410
- Also stated that the trades were part

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:43.110
of a larger purchase that included

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:45.500
a lot of stock that has
subsequently gone down.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:48.290
- There's a range of different decisions

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:52.250
made every day with regard to
my savings and 401k portfolios

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:53.770
that I'm not involved in,

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.325
and certainly, like any other trades,

00:16:56.325 --> 00:16:58.490
you can't see into the future.

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:00.590
- Burr, however, doesn't
deny making the trades,

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:02.810
but says he did so on public information,

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:05.357
and his general concern for
the impact of the coronavirus.

00:17:05.357 --> 00:17:07.717
The specific statement he released stated,

00:17:07.717 --> 00:17:10.117
"I relied solely on public
news reports to guide

00:17:10.117 --> 00:17:12.837
"my decision regarding the sale
of stocks on February 13th.

00:17:12.837 --> 00:17:15.637
"Specifically, I closely
followed CNBC's daily health

00:17:15.637 --> 00:17:18.917
"and science reporting out of
its Asia bureaus at the time.

00:17:18.917 --> 00:17:21.257
"Understanding the assumption
many could make in hindsight,

00:17:21.257 --> 00:17:23.127
"however, I spoke this
morning with the chairman

00:17:23.127 --> 00:17:25.097
"of the Senate Ethics
Committee and asked him

00:17:25.097 --> 00:17:26.797
"to open a complete review of the matter

00:17:26.797 --> 00:17:28.460
"with full transparency."

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:29.960
Now, it's possible both of these things

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.510
could be a complete defense.

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:34.640
If Loeffler can show
that she never contacted

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:37.670
the third parties who made
the trades on her behalf,

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:41.240
then it seems unlikely that they colluded

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:44.440
in some fashion to trade
on inside information,

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:48.460
and if Burr can somehow
show that he never used

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:51.090
confidential information
in making those trades,

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.660
that might be a defense as well.

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:55.640
But everyone has to sort
of admit that the timing

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:58.480
on these trades is highly suspicious.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.930
Now, if the allegations are true,

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:04.500
and the implications
turn out to be correct,

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.140
Burr and Loeffler put their
portfolio above the safety

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:08.730
and well-being of their fellow Americans

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:11.580
that they were voted in to represent,

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.830
and they would deserve more
significant consequences

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.380
than simply not being reelected.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:18.170
They would need to be held
accountable for their actions.

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:21.010
But beyond that, I think
Congress needs to further rethink

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:24.700
the restrictions on how they're
allowed to invest in office.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.840
The situation also goes to show

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:29.420
the benefit of having a blind trust.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:31.670
A valid argument could
be made that congressmen

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.030
and women should never
be active investors,

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:37.750
but really should only be
allowed to be passively invested

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:40.080
in ways in which they
cannot gain from the use

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:42.290
of their classified or
non-public information.

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:45.910
In a blind trust the owner
or trustor of the assets

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.800
in theory has no knowledge of the specific

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:49.640
stock holdings in the trust.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:52.550
The only control the
trustor has over the trustee

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:55.110
is to initiate the trust
and to terminate it.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:58.720
But having that blind trust
would inoculate the senators

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:01.080
from these kind of
allegations that they profited

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.150
over classified information
that they received.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:06.570
This would obviously be a
burden to congresspeople

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:08.930
and senators, but you
know, if you're elected

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:12.722
to the highest deliberative
body in the country,

00:19:12.722 --> 00:19:15.880
you probably need to make some sacrifices

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:17.260
in order to hold that office.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.570
But in an interesting
coda to this whole thing,

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:21.710
the report to the SEC will in fact

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:24.010
investigate these transactions.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.100
So we actually may learn more about

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.360
these suspicious trades after all.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:30.660
You would think that these
congresspeople would be better

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.080
at business and wouldn't need
to use classified information

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:35.280
to make a buck at the public's expense.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:37.550
Instead of using their
positions for personal gain,

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:39.850
they should really take Michael
Chernow's Skillshare class

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:43.820
Entrepreneurship Hustle, From
Business Plan to Real Success.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:46.230
Michael would teach these
senators how to find

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:48.390
market opportunity, nail
their business plan,

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:50.550
pitch investors, align brand and culture,

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:52.380
and measure success, you know,

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:55.020
in a way that isn't dollars
made shorting the market

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:56.980
before the coronavirus shuts it down.

00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:58.710
And if they're committing insider trading

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:00.170
because they're bad with money,

